---
/**
 * Early access (marketing-site story 3): what it means, and the sign-up form.
 * The form posts nowhere until `lead-capture` wires `POST /api/leads`.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import LeadForm from "../components/LeadForm.astro";
import { h1, link, prose } from "../lib/ui";
---

<Base
  title="Early access"
  description="What early access to Wipestation means, and the sign-up form. Sign-up is not open yet, and the form sends nothing."
>
  <h1 class={h1}>Early access</h1>
  <div class={prose}>
    <p>
      Early access means trying pre-release builds of Wipestation before launch and helping decide
      what ships first. Every pre-release build runs against simulated drives: four virtual
      devices with progress and evidence generated in software. No real storage hardware is
      involved yet.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is for ITAD operators, enterprise IT refresh teams and government buyers who want to see
      the certificate, the evidence and the bench workflow early, and tell us what is missing.
      Early-access pricing is on request; see <a href="/pricing/" class={link}>pricing</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Until sign-up opens, the <a href="/capabilities/" class={link}>capabilities page</a> shows
      what is in development and what is planned.
    </p>
  </div>
  <LeadForm kind="early-access" />
</Base>
